<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Ramla</h1><p class="st-meta">1120 CE – 1187 CE (approx.) · capital Ramla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A lordship on the coastal plain of the Kingdom of Jerusalem that became a power base of the Ibelin family.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a>, the former capital of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, was occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> in 1099. It was under royal control at first and became a lordship around 1120, held by a family whose heiress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvis-of-ramla">Helvis</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan of Ibelin</a>, bringing it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelins</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> and the nearby castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirabel-castle">Mirabel</a> controlled the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and rich farmland. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ibelin">Ibelin</a> lords Hugh and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-of-ibelin">Baldwin of Ibelin</a> held it in the later 12th century; Baldwin was among the barons who fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montgisard">Montgisard</a> nearby in 1177. In 1186 he refused to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a> as king and left for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-antioch">Antioch</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1187. The title was revived but the lordship was never again held by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> in any lasting way.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="crusader state, 1120 CE – 1187 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">crusader state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.99%;width:1.33%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1120 CE – 1187 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ramla</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hugh of Ibelin, Baldwin of Ibelin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ramla and Mirabel</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1154&amp;focus=lordship-of-ramla" aria-label="Lordship of Ramla on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5578 1016 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Ramla lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5898 1272L5908 1277M5898 1272L5811 1337"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5898 1272h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5898 1272h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ramla. <a href="/atlas?year=1154&amp;focus=lordship-of-ramla">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

